Day 05 - Linux Troubleshooting Runbook

## Target Service
SSH Service


# Environment Check

## 1. uname -a
Shows system information.

```bash
uname -a

2. cat /etc/os-release
Shows Linux version details.
Bash
cat /etc/os-release
File System Check

3. mkdir /tmp/runbook-demo
Creates test folder.
Bash
mkdir /tmp/runbook-demo

4. cp /etc/hosts /tmp/runbook-demo/hosts-copy
Copies file for practice.
Bash
cp /etc/hosts /tmp/runbook-demo/hosts-copy
ls -l /tmp/runbook-demo
Observation: Folder and file created successfully.
CPU & Memory Check

5. top
Checks CPU and memory usage.
Bash
top
Observation: CPU and memory usage looked normal.

6. free -h
Shows RAM usage.
Bash
free -h
Observation: System had available free memory.
Disk Check

7. df -h
Shows disk space usage.
Bash
df -h
Observation: Disk space was sufficient.
Network Check

8. ss -tulpn
Shows listening ports and services.
Bash
ss -tulpn
Observation: SSH service port was active.
Log Check

9. journalctl -u ssh -n 20
Shows SSH service logs.
Bash
journalctl -u ssh -n 20
Observation: No recent errors found in logs.

Quick Findings

System resources were stable
SSH service was running properly
No major errors found in logs
If This Worsens
Restart SSH service
Check detailed logs
Monitor CPU and memory continuously

